llection software deployed to improve tenant arrears recovery","lead":"Tenant arrears collection rate directly affects HRA cash position and determines whether business plan income assumptions are met","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"Rent convergence approved: rises of CPI+1%+\u00a31 from April 2027 and CPI+1%+\u00a32 from 2028/29","lead":"Rent increases are a material change to revenue assumptions affecting HRA business plan viability and cash generation","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true},{"headline":"HRA capital investment now set at upper limit within affordability constraints from 2027/28","lead":"Affordability constraint on capital limits the council's ability to invest in housing maintenance and signals financial tension in the HRA","iso":"2026-09-22","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","byline":"PWLBintel \u00b7 from committee papers","draft":true}],"findings":[{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","headline":"Additional staffing and rent collection software deployed to improve tenant arrears recovery","detail":"A new staffing post has been created and rent collection software implementation is underway. A former tenant arrears officer is in post using external tracing agencies to pursue arrears. The council is also purchasing a rent analytics tool using predictive payment profiling to target income collection efforts.","category":"income","matters":"Tenant arrears collection rate directly affects HRA cash position and determines whether business plan income assumptions are met","figures":"None","quote":"Additional staffing post and implementation of rent collection software underway","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","headline":"Rent convergence approved: rises of CPI+1%+\u00a31 from April 2027 and CPI+1%+\u00a32 from 2028/29","detail":"Cabinet has approved rent convergence in budget setting proposals from 2027/28. Rents will increase at CPI plus 1% plus \u00a31 for the year 2027/28 and CPI plus 1% plus \u00a32 from 2028/29 onwards. Modelling is underway to quantify the additional income impact.","category":"income","matters":"Rent increases are a material change to revenue assumptions affecting HRA business plan viability and cash generation","figures":"CPI +1% +\u00a31 for 2027/28 and CPI+1%+\u00a32 from 2028/29","quote":"This is Consumer Prices Index (CPI) +1% +\u00a31 for 2027/28 and CPI+1%+\u00a32 from 2028/29.","material":false},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","headline":"HRA capital investment now set at upper limit within affordability constraints from 2027/28","detail":"Capital investment programme will be limited to an upper bound and set at an affordable level from 2027/28 onwards. The annual investment target is circa \u00a35m, established within defined affordability levels based on Stock Condition Survey analysis.","category":"capital","matters":"Affordability constraint on capital limits the council's ability to invest in housing maintenance and signals financial tension in the HRA","figures":"circa \u00a35m","quote":"Capital investment programme will be set at an upper limit and at an affordable level from 2027/28","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","headline":"External experts have completed review of 30-year business plan and HRA debt financing","detail":"Savills has reviewed the HRA 30-year business plan, updating forecast assumptions for key indices. The council's treasury advisors have completed review of HRA debt financing. Both reviews have been completed and findings incorporated.","category":"governance","matters":"Independent validation of business plan and debt sustainability provides lender assurance of plan robustness","figures":"None","quote":"2 external reviews have been undertaken. Savills to review the 30 year business plan and the Councils treasury advisors to review the HRA debt financing.","material":true},{"iso":"2026-09-22","committee":"Finance and Economic Overview and Scrutiny Committee","paper_title":"AppendixCHRAActionPlanAugust2026","paper_url":"https://moderngov.southkesteven.gov.uk/documents/s52494/52494.pdf","headline":"Significant capital programme budget variances triggered implementation of new controls to prevent future overspends","detail":"The council experienced 'significant budget variances in the capital programme' which prompted the introduction of spending controls. Orders can now only be raised where budget is available and require virements approved per Financial Regulations. The policy now states: no further overspends against individual schemes are permitted.","category":"capital","matters":"Budget variances indicate prior control weakness; new preventive controls are essential reassurance for lenders","figures":"None","quote":"In response to significant budget variances in the capital programme, undertake regular budget virements to ensure orders can only be raised where there is budget availability","material":true}],"editorial":null,"freshness":{"last_paper_iso":"2026-07-30"},"name":"South Kesteven","findings_total":77,"news_drafts_total":3}}